From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: honour an explicit local Japanese XP Luna font profile

Purpose: give the XP shell the fonts that Japanese XP reports, where Wine's
parsing of the theme file cannot.
XP behavior: public GetThemeFont and SPI calls on the Japanese XP reference
(tests/theme-props.c, tests/taskbar-fonts.c) report MS UI Gothic for the
system fonts, TaskBand::Toolbar at -12 (part zero, normal and checked),
the Clock, the StartPanel user name (-19 bold) and More Programs (-12 bold).
Change: read user-owned LOGFONT values from
HKCU\Software\Win4Wine\ThemeProfiles\JapaneseXPLuna (Enabled and Version 1,
matching theme path, colour and size, values at 96 DPI) for these
class/part/state queries and the six system fonts, which are applied
through the existing theme metrics save and classic restore. Missing or
invalid values keep the original result; the DLL contains no font names.
Evidence: tests/font-profile.c at 96, 144 and 192 DPI, with and without the
opt-in, disabled, missing and invalid profiles.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL and the matching active theme.
Old patches: 0026, 0035, 0040, 0057 (its font profile part).
---
